WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.919
The four jobs of a manager. Every manager, in every part of Vanderbilt, does the same four jobs every week.

2
00:00:08.969 --> 00:00:15.714
Job one, get the work done: plan it, say what good looks like, check it before it is due,

3
00:00:15.764 --> 00:00:18.233
and fix the cause when it breaks.

4
00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:24.111
Job two, take care of your people: listen, grow them, thank them, trust them.

5
00:00:24.161 --> 00:00:32.357
Job three, make things better: explain the why, describe where the team is going, let people try, look back.

6
00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:39.380
Job four, connect your team to the rest of Vanderbilt: know the people your team depends on,

7
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.121
watch for what is coming, speak up for your team.

8
00:00:43.171 --> 00:00:51.366
Nothing here is new work. It is the same work, sorted, and the assessment you took scores these same habits.

9
00:00:51.416 --> 00:00:55.413
The skill is noticing which job this week needs most.

10
00:00:55.463 --> 00:01:00.451
For example: a facilities supervisor starts Monday with four asks.

11
00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:06.025
A backlog of work orders. A new technician who wants to learn the boiler.

12
00:01:06.075 --> 00:01:11.063
A new work-order system. And Events asking for his crew on Friday.

13
00:01:11.113 --> 00:01:16.865
One list, four different jobs. Sorting it tells him where the week is heavy.

14
00:01:16.915 --> 00:01:20.606
This week: sort your own list into the four jobs.

